  "pluginAutomation": {
    "$comment": "The fixed automation-slot map plugin hosts see (issue #121; design note in packages/vst3/README.md). Hosts require the parameter list declared once at construction with IDs that persist across sessions, but core rigs are dynamic grids addressed by (block_id, index) - so slots mediate: slot 0 is permanently the master bus, slots 1..slotCount-1 bind to live blocks and are part of the serialized rig state. Each slot exposes paramsPerSlot generic entries whose meaning/range/unit resolve dynamically from whatever block is bound (hosts get title-change notifications on rebind). paramsPerSlot must be >= every kind/variant's param count below - the generator validates that and fails otherwise; it is deliberately a frozen stride (20 today, headroom over reverb-hall's 18), because changing it remaps every host parameter id. Values cross this boundary normalized 0..1 and map linearly onto each resolved param's min/max.",
    "slotCount": 16,
    "paramsPerSlot": 20,
    "masterSlot": {
      "$comment": "Slot 0's fixed descriptors - never rebound, never serialized (the master bus itself already rides the document as masterLevel/masterMuted). 'default' is the native-unit default used to derive the host-facing normalized default; level mirrors the web Master knob (GridEditor.tsx max=1.5 default=1).",
      "params": [
        {
          "symbol": "level",
          "label": "Master Level",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1.5,
          "unit": "x",
          "default": 1
